course: dictionary
lesson: 4359
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. The word gummy is a good example. «Gummy sweets are made by squirting hot syrup into shapes.» Here gummy means a chewy sweet.
explain: «The baby gave a gummy grin.» A baby has no teeth yet, so the grin shows lots of gum, the pink part above the teeth. Here gummy describes the gum, not a sweet. Always ask which meaning fits the words around it.
explain: Gummy can also mean sticky, like glue or gum. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
fact: Gummy means sticky, like glue or gum.
fact: A gummy smile shows a lot of gum, the pink part above the teeth.
fact: A gummy is a chewy sweet, like a gummy bear or a gummy worm.
fact: «Gummy vitamins» look like sweets, so keep them out of reach of small children and take only the dose on the packet.
fact: One word can have several meanings, so always look at the words around it.
exercise: «Gummy bears are poured into shapes pressed in trays of cornflour.» What is a gummy bear? | A tooth that has come out | A large toy from a shop | A brown bear that lives in the woods | *A chewy sweet
exercise: «The baby gave a gummy grin, with no teeth at all.» What does gummy mean here? | A sweet made of sugar | Shiny and bright | Very loud | *Showing a lot of gum, with no teeth
exercise: «Her fingers were gummy after the sticky syrup.» What does gummy mean? | Hungry | *Sticky, like glue | Cold and wet | Clean and dry
test: «The table was gummy from the spilt juice.» What does gummy mean? | Round and smooth | *Sticky, like glue | Very heavy | Icy cold
test: Ella says gummy always means a sweet. What is the right answer? | No, gummy means very fast | *Gummy can mean a sweet, but it can also mean sticky or showing no teeth | Yes, gummy only ever means a sweet | Gummy is only a name for a dog
exam: Which meaning fits best in «The gummy bears were on sale at the shop»? | Very old | *A chewy sweet | Showing no teeth | Sticky like glue
